<header class="rm-head"><h1>Review updated plan terms</h1><p>Your subscription price and billing date stay the same. Your existing records and usage history stay in place.</p></header>
<section class="rm-panel"><div class="rm-panel__head"><h2><%= terms.subscription.plan_name %></h2></div><div class="card-body"><p>New AI requests use the updated work-credit definition. A typical question uses 20 credits; files and complex work can use more. Previous usage stays recorded at its original amount.</p><div class="table-scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Allowance</th><th>Current terms</th><th>Updated terms</th></tr></thead><tbody><% for(const m of terms.next.meters.filter(m=>m.included_units!==undefined)){const before=terms.current.meters.find(x=>x.meter===m.meter); %><tr><td><%= m.label %></td><td><%= before?.included_units==null?'Unlimited':Number(before.included_units).toLocaleString() %></td><td><%= m.included_units==null?'Unlimited':Number(m.included_units).toLocaleString() %></td></tr><% } %></tbody></table></div><p>If an existing inventory exceeds a new capacity limit, its records stay available; adding more is paused until capacity is available. Unused included AI credits carry for one month under the updated terms.</p><% if(terms.changed){ %><form method="post" action="/billing/terms"><input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>"><input type="hidden" name="currentVersion" value="<%= terms.current.id %>"><input type="hidden" name="nextVersion" value="<%= terms.next.id %>"><label><input type="checkbox" name="confirm" value="1" required> I accept these updated allowances and the work-credit definition.</label><div class="form-actions"><button class="rm-btn">Accept updated terms</button><a class="rm-btn rm-btn--ghost" href="/billing">Keep my current terms</a></div></form><% }else{ %><p>You already have the current terms.</p><a class="rm-btn" href="/billing">Back to billing</a><% } %></div></section>
